{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7HSqszEuKGNCrn69Si6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the draft below. It comes to about 250 words with the brackets filled in. Three of your facts could hurt the application if the summary skipped them, so I wrote around them and left brackets where only you have the answer.\n\n<final_document>\n**Project Summary**\n\n[Clinic Name] requests $90,000 over two years ($45,000 per year) to add a third staff attorney to our eviction defense practice.\n\n**Need.** Last year, 1,140 eviction cases were filed in [County]. Our two attorneys represented the tenant in 163 of them, about one in seven. We turned away roughly 300 more tenants who asked for help because no attorney was free. Each of our attorneys carries about 80 open cases, so we cannot take on more without more staff.\n\n**Results.** In the cases where we represented the tenant last year, 58% ended with the tenant staying in the home or getting at least 60 days to move. [Optional: one sentence on how, such as negotiated agreements, procedural defenses or rental assistance applications.]\n\n**Project.** A third attorney would let us represent about 80 more tenants a year once fully trained, or about a quarter of the tenants we now turn away. [Optional: which cases the new attorney would prioritize, such as families with children, subsidized housing or tenants with disabilities.]\n\n**Budget and sustainability.** The position costs $78,000 a year including benefits. Foundation funds would cover $45,000 a year, and the remaining $33,000 a year will come from [source]. Our core operations are supported by a $60,000 annual contract with [County], [renewed in October through ____ / up for renewal in October 2027]. One of our current attorneys leaves in June. We will fill that position with [source], so this grant adds a third attorney rather than replacing one.\n</final_document>\n\n**What you need to fill in:**\n\n1. **The $33,000 a year gap.** The foundation will see right away that its maximum award doesn't cover the salary. You need to name where the rest comes from, or say the position will be part-time. The award is per year, so you can't make up the difference by asking for more in total.\n2. **The attorney leaving in June.** If that position isn't refilled, this grant gets you back to two attorneys, not three. Calling it a \"third attorney\" would then be inaccurate, and the foundation would likely find out. If you can't yet say how you'll refill it, the project should be described honestly as keeping your current capacity, which is still a fundable request.\n3. **The county contract.** It's now November, so if the renewal was due last month, give the result. A funder will notice an \"up for renewal\" date that has already passed.\n\n**Other choices I made:**\n- **The 58% result.** I stated it plainly and didn't compare it to tenants without lawyers, since you don't have that number.\n- **The \"about 80 more tenants\" estimate.** It comes from your own numbers: 163 cases between two attorneys is about 80 each per year. A new hire will take time to reach that caseload, which is why the draft says \"once fully trained.\""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5415,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5415},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a264e9d9-889d-4308-82a6-dba9d30368ef","uuid":"e6d6029b-85b5-46b8-ba79-3dabc1fe6589","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:03:58.288Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7HSqiL3MweLiEUeu553"}
